Score the emotional sentiment of each numbered conversation turn below.

For every turn return:
- "turn_index": the integer index given,
- "score": a float in [-1.0, 1.0] (negative = upset/frustrated/sad, 0 = neutral, positive = warm/pleased/enthusiastic),
- "label": one short lowercase word for the dominant emotion (e.g. neutral, frustrated, pleased, anxious, confident, sad, curious).

Judge only what the words convey; do not invent context. Return JSON only:
{"turns": [{"turn_index": 0, "score": 0.0, "label": "neutral"}, ...]}

TURNS:
{% for t in turns %}
[{{ t.turn_index }}] {{ t.role }}: {{ t.content }}
